.SS "uint32_t(* schultz_selectable_vtable::offset_at) (\fBschultz_tree\fP *tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_point\fP local)"
Which byte offset a point lands on, in the node's own coordinates\&.
.PP
Used when a drag arrives over this node\&. An offset past the end is the end, and a point above the first line is the beginning, so a drag that leaves the node still gives a sensible answer\&. 
.PP
