.SS "void(* schultz_selectable_vtable::set_range) (\fBschultz_tree\fP *tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, uint32_t low, uint32_t high)"
Marks the bytes from \fClow\fP up to but not including \fChigh\fP as selected\&.
.PP
Equal values mean nothing here is selected, which is what every node outside the range is told\&. Called whenever the range moves, so it is expected to be cheap and to repaint only when something changed\&. 
.PP
